@startuml project-workspace
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Per-run Docker volume and full-clone lifecycle (FR-07)
caption A new run gets a new volume and independent clone; an interrupted SAME run recovers its existing volume.

state Entry <<choice>>
state "Resolve configured project\nTask project -> repository identity\nConfigured remote and target branch" as Resolve
state "Verify repository access and identity\nRead target branch/commit and project guidance\nExpose resolved target to the user" as Inspect
state "Repository resolved\nReturn configuration revision + target snapshot" as Resolved <<success>>

state "Verify claim and prior task ownership\nTask/run IDs, repository + target revision\nPrior run closed or explicitly blocked" as Claim
state "Reserve unique Docker volume + branch\nPersist creation intent, run/ticket IDs and lease\nNo agent chooses isolation" as Reserve
state BranchSource <<choice>>
state "Create named volume and full clone\nStart task branch at verified target commit\nMount only into this run's container" as Clone
state "Create named volume and full clone\nFetch verified saved remote branch\nFor NEW run after review/dependency" as Saved
state "Verify volume and clone\nDB reference, Docker identity/labels and manifest agree\nOrigin, branch, HEAD, lease and expected files" as Verify
state "Workspace ready for run\nPersist volume ID, branch, commit and manifest\nCaller may start container, then Jira/preflight" as Ready <<success>>

state "Recheck mounted clone before code\nAccepted spec, target/base, volume lease\nBranch/HEAD and expected manifest" as BeforeCode
state "Code workspace ready\nPermit bounded agent assignments" as CodeReady <<success>>
state "Repeat preflight\nTask/target inputs moved" as Recheck <<attention>>

state "Inspect volume at run end\nAll executors stopped/fenced\nCheck committed, staged, untracked and ignored task data" as EndInspect
state "Remove safe run volume\nAll necessary work published or durably preserved\nVerify Docker removal and journal disposition" as Remove
state "Retain run volume for recovery\nPersist complete state manifest and owner\nBlock same-task new run until reconciled" as Retain
state "Volume retired" as Retired <<success>>
state "Volume retained under task ownership" as Retained <<attention>>
state "Cleanup incomplete\nWriter/volume/effects unresolved\nKeep claim and slot until safe" as CleanupPending <<attention>>
state "Needs attention\nMissing mapping, unsafe ownership or clone failure" as Attention <<attention>>

[*] --> Entry
Entry --> Resolve : [resolve_for_admission]
Entry --> Claim : [create_for_run; claim + slot persisted]
Entry --> BeforeCode : [verify_for_code]
Entry --> EndInspect : [end_run]
Resolve --> Inspect : one explicit configured repository found
Resolve --> Attention : missing/ambiguous mapping or target
Inspect --> Resolved : identity, access and target verified
Inspect --> Attention : wrong repository or inaccessible inputs
Resolved --> [*] : return repository_ready
Claim --> Reserve : current owner; prior run reconciled
Claim --> Attention : stale claim or prior run unresolved
Reserve --> BranchSource : unique volume ID/lease + intent persisted
Reserve --> Attention : conflict or ambiguous creation / reconcile first
BranchSource --> Clone : [no saved remote branch]
BranchSource --> Saved : [verified saved remote branch]
Clone --> Verify : clone and checkout returned
Saved --> Verify : clone and checkout returned
Clone --> Attention : clone failed or effect ambiguous / inspect volume
Saved --> Attention : saved ref missing or effect ambiguous
Verify --> Ready : DB, Docker, manifest and Git evidence match
Verify --> Attention : mismatch, unexpected files or lease conflict
Ready --> [*] : return workspace_ready
BeforeCode --> CodeReady : spec and volume/clone evidence current
BeforeCode --> Recheck : task or target/base changed
BeforeCode --> Attention : volume missing, shared or unexpectedly changed
CodeReady --> [*] : return code_workspace_ready
Recheck --> [*] : return recheck_preflight
EndInspect --> Remove : clean or all changes published/preserved
EndInspect --> Retain : dirty state captured; owner fenced
EndInspect --> CleanupPending : cannot fence, classify or capture
Remove --> Retired : removal confirmed
Remove --> CleanupPending : removal uncertain / reconcile first
Retain --> Retained : manifest + recovery block persisted
Retain --> CleanupPending : retention unconfirmed
CleanupPending --> EndInspect : bounded reconciliation restores certainty
Retired --> [*] : return volume_retired
Retained --> [*] : return volume_retained
Attention --> [*] : return attention

note right of Verify
  The volume is persistent Docker storage on this host,
  independent of the disposable task container layer.
  Database identity is authoritative; Docker labels and
  the volume manifest corroborate it. No match, no mount.
end note
note bottom of Retained
  Same-run recovery remounts this exact volume only after
  fencing and checkpoint/effect reconciliation. A later NEW
  run gets a NEW volume and clones a verified saved remote
  branch; it never inherits the old container or sessions.
  A volume on this host does not protect against disk loss.
end note
@enduml
